{"body":{"value":"\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-problem-motivation\u0022\u003EMotivation\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-php\u0022\u003EManagedFile::uploadAjaxCallback() \u003C\/code\u003Erenders a status_messages element into the replaced widget\u0027s #prefix and ships it inside the \u003Ccode class=\u0022language-php\u0022\u003Einsert\u003C\/code\u003E AJAX command. It should use the AJAX MessageCommand instead, which has been introduced with Drupal 8.8 - see \u003Ca href=\u0022https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/node\/3086403\u0022 rel=\u0022nofollow\u0022\u003Echange record\u003C\/a\u003E.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis solves a couple of things:\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E1. Atm, this server-rendered messages use AJAX insert command and thus go via XSS filtering, stripping things like Olivero\u0027s SVG message icon. There is dedicated bug report for this \u003Cspan class=\u0022project-issue-issue-link project-issue-status-info project-issue-status-1\u0022\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022\/project\/drupal\/issues\/3457067\u0022 title=\u0022Status: Active\u0022\u003E#3457067: Status messages rendered in managed file form elements filter HTML too aggressively\u003C\/a\u003E\u003C\/span\u003E, which this issue would resolve.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E2. Accessibility: Messages rendered via the AJAX message command are properly using aria live announcements, previously it relied on inline markup adding a \u003Ccode class=\u0022language-php\u0022\u003Erole=\u0022alert\u0022 \u003C\/code\u003E markup or similar. Live announcements is the way to do this right.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E3. Flexible placement: Atm errors appear inside the file widget, between the Save button and the field, instead of the theme\u0027s message region where every other message goes. The \u003Ccode class=\u0022language-php\u0022\u003EMessageCommand\u003C\/code\u003E supports both, via the \u003Ccode class=\u0022language-php\u0022\u003EwrapperQuerySelector\u003C\/code\u003E - so we can decide what is preferred UX wise. Note: For better backwards compatibility, I\u0027ve kept it within the widget in the attached MR.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E4. By giving the theme the control to render the message, it allows decoupled rendering to render it nicely also. -\u0026gt; I\u0027m using this for making support of ajax file uploads in Drupal-forms embedded in lupus-decoupled frontends nice. \u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-steps-reproduce\u0022\u003ESteps to reproduce\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDrupal 11.4, standard install, Olivero, content type with a file field.\u003C\/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EOn the node form, upload a file exceeding the limit.\u003C\/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EThe error renders inside the widget and the page message region stays empty.\u003C\/li\u003E\n\u003C\/ul\u003E\n\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-proposed-resolution\u0022\u003EProposed resolution\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAdopt the AJAX MessageCommand.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-ui-changes\u0022\u003EUser interface changes\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWhen uploading a file via the core #managed_file element and errors occur, the error messages are rendered via the themes\u0027 implementation of the MessageCommand, not via server-rendered messages. This might be slightly different, depending on the theme.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-introduced-terminology\u0022\u003EIntroduced terminology\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E-\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-api-changes\u0022\u003EAPI changes\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E-\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3 id=\u0022summary-data-model-changes\u0022\u003EData model changes\u003C\/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E-\u003C\/p\u003E","summary":"","format":"1"},"taxonomy_vocabulary_9":[{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/taxonomy_term\/1101","id":"1101","resource":"taxonomy_term"}],"field_issue_status":"16","field_issue_priority":"200","field_issue_category":"2","field_issue_component":"file.module","field_project":{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/node\/3060","id":"3060","resource":"node","machine_name":"drupal"},"field_issue_files":[{"file":{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/file\/7177454","id":"7177454","resource":"file","cid":"16740329"},"display":"1"},{"file":{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/file\/7178048","id":"7178048","resource":"file","cid":"16744581"},"display":"1"},{"file":{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/file\/7178049","id":"7178049","resource":"file","cid":"16744581"},"display":"1"}],"field_issue_related":[{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/node\/3086096","id":"3086096","resource":"node"},{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/node\/3081526","id":"3081526","resource":"node"},{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/node\/3457067","id":"3457067","resource":"node"}],"field_issue_version":"main","field_issue_last_status_change":"1790907578","field_issue_parent_link":[],"field_issue_related_links":[{"url":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/node\/3086096","attributes":[],"display_url":null},{"url":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/node\/3081526","attributes":[],"display_url":null},{"url":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/node\/3457067","attributes":[],"display_url":null}],"flag_project_issue_follow_user":[{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/user\/456718","id":456718,"resource":"user"},{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/user\/27930","id":27930,"resource":"user"},{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/user\/180064","id":180064,"resource":"user"},{"uri":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/api-d7\/user\/16747","id":16747,"resource":"user"}],"nid":"3618230","vid":"14508713","is_new":false,"type":"project_issue","title":"Adopt the ajax MessageCommand for file uploads","language":"en","url":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/project\/drupal\/issues\/3618230","edit_url":"https:\/\/www.drupal.org\/node\/3618230\/edit","status":"1","promote":"0","sticky":"0","created":"1787212050","changed":"1790907578","author":{"uri"